From 61b05a136c9280d10ce0d52405a30a7d6fa18b06 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pystartup <pystartup@localhost>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 01:44:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [startup] opt-in worker zygote: fork TP workers from a
 preloaded fork server

With SGLANG_WORKER_ZYGOTE=1 the launch process starts a multiprocessing fork server
at the top of `import sglang`. It preloads the CUDA-free import set in parallel with
the launch process, under a guard that serves device facts from an NVML probe and
trips on any other way into the driver. Workers are forked from it only if torch.cuda
is uninitialised, no /dev/nvidia* fd is open and it runs one thread; otherwise spawn
is kept. Each worker gets the launch process's environment as of Process.start().

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
